# FraudLens: AI-Powered Fraud Detection & Risk Intelligence Platform

> 🚧 **Status: In Progress**

FraudLens is an end-to-end fraud analytics platform built on the PaySim
mobile-money transaction dataset (~6.36M rows, 0.13% fraud). It covers data
engineering, analytics, machine learning, and an LLM-based investigator agent.

## Goals

- Build an ETL pipeline with pandas, NumPy, and PySpark
- Store and query data on AWS (S3, Athena)
- Analyze fraud patterns with SQL and a Power BI dashboard
- Detect fraud with Random Forest, Isolation Forest, and a TensorFlow autoencoder
- Segment accounts with K-Means and validate patterns with hypothesis tests
- Build an LLM agent (SQL + scoring tools) that investigates accounts and exports an Excel case report
- Implement the Union-Find fraud-ring detector in Java

## Tech Stack

Python, SQL, Java (basic), PySpark, pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn,
TensorFlow, Power BI, Excel, AWS, Git

## Dataset

PaySim synthetic mobile-money transactions (Kaggle).

